Title: React Project — ProjectRole

Stack & Versions
- React 18 + TypeScript, Vite, pnpm.
- Router: react-router-dom.
- Data: @tanstack/react-query.
- Forms/Validation: react-hook-form + zod.
- State: Zustand (light), Context for cross-cutting concerns.
- Tests: vitest + @testing-library/react + @testing-library/user-event.
- Lint/Format: ESLint (TS, React, hooks, import), Prettier.

Architecture & Structure
- Use a feature-first structure for anything beyond trivial:
  src/
    app/               # app shell, routing, providers
    features/          # vertical slices (auth, tasks, profile…)
    entities/          # domain models (user, task…), adapters
    shared/            # ui (atoms), lib (utils), config, hooks
    widgets/           # composed UI blocks
- Use "@/..." import alias. No deep relative import spaghetti.

Conventions
- Components: PascalCase, 1 component per file when possible.
- Hooks: useCamelCase, colocate with feature.
- Exports: named exports; index.ts for barrel if logical.
- Avoid default exports for utilities/hooks.
- File naming: kebab-case for files, PascalCase for component files.
- CSS: Tailwind preferred; minimal CSS modules if needed. No inline styles except rapid prototypes.
- Comments: English only.

API & Data Layer
- Fetch with React Query. Define query keys in a central module.
- Keep API adapters pure and typed; no UI logic inside.
- Zod for runtime validation of external data. Narrow types based on parsed schema.
- Global error handling: network errors -> toast/alert + retry button where relevant.

Env & Config
- All client envs must be prefixed with VITE_. Provide safe defaults for local dev.
- Do not hardcode secrets.
- Provide example .env.example whenever new envs are introduced.

UX, A11y, i18n
- Loading skeletons or spinners; handle empty states.
- Keyboard accessibility and aria-* for interactive elements.
- Keep strings centralized for future i18n.

Performance
- Split heavy routes/widgets via lazy() + Suspense.
- Memoize expensive selectors; prefer React Query caching over ad-hoc global state.
- Watch bundle size; avoid large deps unless justified.

Testing
- Unit: vitest for utils and hooks.
- Component tests with RTL: cover success/loading/error/empty.
- Write tests for bug fixes (regression safety).

CI & Quality Gates (local are fine too)
- Lint and test must pass before merge.
- Pre-commit: lint-staged runs prettier & eslint --fix on staged files.

Deliverables When Generating Code
- Provide full file contents with path headers, e.g. “src/features/auth/api.ts”.
- Include new deps and install command: pnpm add … / pnpm add -D …
- Provide minimal tests where appropriate.
- If touching routing or providers, show changes in src/app/main.tsx or src/app/routes.tsx.

Examples of Common Scaffolds
- Page with data fetch: create route, query hook, component with states (loading/error/empty/data).
- Form: RHF + Zod schema, typed submit handler, inline error messaging, happy-path test.
- Zustand store: typed state/actions, no side effects in reducers.
